3. f4 ( { a) If } 3. h5 { then } Be8 $1 { heading for b5; e.g. } 4. f4 ( { a1) neither } 4. Kc3 Ke5 ) 
 ( { a2) nor } 4. Ke3 Kc4 { is any better; } ) 
Bb5 5. Ke3 ( { a3) or } 5. Kc3 Be2 $1 ) 
Bd7 6. Kf3 ( { a4) the attempt at a theoretical draw by } 6. f5 Ke5 7. g5 Bxf5 8. h6 { fails to } gxh6 9. gxh6 Bh7 { followed by ...Kd4-c3-b2; } ) 
