 { At first sight the position looks about equal - White has fixed his kingside pawns on squares of the 'right' colour, while the black knight feels quite comfortable in such a semi-closed structure. However, Ivanchuk has a surprise prepared. } 1... { -KEY- } f5 $1 { A strong advance that clears a path for the king and softens up White's kingside pawns. } 2. gxf5 ( { Or } 2. Kf2 Nf6 { when } 3. Kg3 { fails to } fxg4 4. fxg4 Ne4 { - Ivanchuk. } ) 
Kf7 3. Bf4 Kf6 ( { Another option was } 3... Nf6 { , but Black prefers to improve his king first. } ) 
4. Be5+ Kxf5 5. Bxg7 Kg5 6. Be5 ( { Perhaps } 6. Kf2 Kxh5 7. Kg3 Kg5 8. Be5 { was a lesser evil - Ivanchuk. } ) 
Kxh5 7. Bb8 a6 { The previous pawn trade definitely favoured Black, who can now enter any pawn ending with confidence, thanks to the outside passed pawn on the h-file. } 8. Kf2 Ng5 9. Kg3 Ne6 10. c3 Kg5 11. Bd6 Kf5 12. a4 $6 ( 12. Bb8 { was more tenacious, when } c5 ( { while } 12. a4 b6 { trying to enhance ...c6-c5, can be met by } 13. Ba7 ) 
13. dxc5 Nxc5 14. Bf4 $1 h5 15. Be3 { is just slightly worse for White - Ivanchuk. } ) 
b6 { Trying to open a new front by ...c6-c5. } 13. b4 $6 { In his eagerness to prevent ...c6-c5, White creates a target for the opponent on c3. } ( { More solid was } 13. Bb8 { intending to meet } c5 14. Ba7 $1 cxd4 15. Bxb6 { although after } dxc3 $1 16. bxc3 Nf4 { Black keeps the advantage - Ivanchuk. } ) 
h5 $1 { Black's actions on the queenside have been limited, so he now resumes play on the opposite flank. } 14. Kf2 ( { a) Worse is } 14. Kh4 Ng5 15. Kxh5 Nxf3 { followed by Ke4-d3. } ) 
 ( { b) Or } 14. Bb8 Nf4 $1 { intending } 15. Bxf4 h4 16. Kxh4 Kxf4 ) 
h4 15. Be7 h3 $1 { The typical function of the outside passed pawn: deflection of the enemy king. } 16. Bd6 $6 ( { The last chance was probably } 16. Kg3 Nf4 17. Bd8 { trying to swap pawns; e.g. } b5 18. axb5 cxb5 19. Bc7 $1 Ne2 20. Kxh3 Nxc3 21. Kg2 { when the bishop prevents the entry of Black's king via f4-e3. } ) 
Nf4 { The weakness on c3 finally takes its toll. } 17. Kg3 Ne2+ 18. Kxh3 Nxc3 19. Kg3 ( { Or } 19. a5 Nb5 $1 20. Be5 bxa5 21. bxa5 c5 { and wins - Ivanchuk. } ) 
Nxa4 20. Bc7 Ke6 21. Kf2 Kd7 22. Bf4 Nc3 23. Ke3 ( { Now Black wins a second pawn; though after } 23. Bd2 Nb5 { preparing ...Nd6-c4, ...Ke6-f5 and ...a6-a5, the victory should only be a question of time. } ) 
Na2 
